  "findings": {
    "259844716": "Original attack involving neutral Spirit actually starts Hand trigger and deferred native Normal Summon. Successful summon doubles original battle participant using source-owned effect, same field identity; attacking/defending, decline/wrong-type, immunity, negated summon, source/Spirit removal and End Phase expiry/original return. Prior nil-return errors and effective omitted-double control retained.",
    "259941091": "Original Oceanica field observer of actual Harmony/Melody/Emma Hand self-summon adds chosen opponent Hand Normal/Special Summon. Deferred Normal Summon now gets ATK0 and immunity; original Special route also protects recipient trigger from Oceanica lock through immunity-aware source-active condition. Decline/no-resource/summon-negation/immunity/leave-and-GY-revival boundaries. GY revival is outside Hand-only lock. Separate missing-ATK/missing-immunity/old-lock controls fail actual outcomes.",
    "metadata": "Harmony226645052/Melody228040066/Emma214349717 each omitted own-Hand location in summon operation info. Exact one-line tp/LOCATION_HAND declarations expose original Oceanica observer for all three; original unmodified reports fail all7 integration cases each. No substituted source activation or API mapping."
  },
  "scope": "Bounded original-effect behavior with actual installed metadata and corrected card-data transport; no Lua API mapping, neutral battle/recipient support only. Not full-card/live Omega certification. Oceanica other-player recovery branch, all-copy/name immunity semantics and remaining source-disabled interactions remain separate audit gaps; do not promote whole card.",
